# ==============================================================================
# sl0ppy Suricata Network Security & Threat Intelligence Dashboard  (v1.2)
# Author : Patrick Hoogeven x0xr00t
# Build  : 07042026
# Name   : SuriDash
# Version: v1.2
# ==============================================================================
# Read-only: nothing in the Suricata configuration is ever modified.
#
# v1.2 changes (on top of v1.1):
#   HARDWARE / VENDOR HEALTH (new section)
#     * Platform auto-detection from DMI (vendor, model, chassis type): IBM,
#       Lenovo (ThinkPad/ThinkCentre/ThinkSystem), Dell, HP/HPE, Fujitsu,
#       Supermicro, Huawei, ASUS, Acer, MSI, Gigabyte, Apple, Oracle/Sun,
#       Toshiba, Samsung, and virtual platforms (QEMU/KVM, VMware, Hyper-V,
#       Xen, VirtualBox).
#     * Vendor toolchain probing (a tool is only used when installed):
#       iprconfig (IBM ServeRAID/ipr), thinkpad-acpi + storcli/OneCLI
#       (Lenovo), hpasmcli/ssacli/hpssacli (HPE), omreport/racadm (Dell),
#       storcli/MegaCli/arcconf (LSI/Broadcom - used by Lenovo, IBM, Dell,
#       Supermicro, Fujitsu OEM controllers), lm-sensors, smartmontools,
#       edac, ipmitool as the generic layer for every vendor.
#     * CPU temperature chain: kernel thermal_zone -> lm-sensors ->
#       ThinkPad ACPI (/proc/acpi/ibm) -> IPMI SDR (the most authoritative
#       source for the platform wins); fan RPM through the same chain.
#     * Battery status / charge / wear % (Lenovo ThinkPad, all laptops via
#       /sys/class/power_supply), CPU frequency + thermal cap detection.
#     * SMART health scan of every sd*/nvme* disk (-n standby: sleeping
#       disks are never spun up), RAID controller status, EDAC memory
#       CE/UE error counts, IPMI SEL tail, hardware health score with
#       HW_TEMP_WARN / HW_TEMP_CRIT thresholds.
#     * SMART_ENABLED / IPMI_ENABLED switches; deep probes (SMART/RAID/SEL)
#       run on the slow refresh cadence, cheap /sys probes every cycle.
#     * Virtual machines are detected and annotated (host passthrough note).
#
# v1.2 changes (on top of v1.1):
#   LIVE TOTAL COUNTERS (update EVERY cycle, i.e. every 2s by default)
#     * "Total pkts (live)" / "Total bytes (live)" in the header: exact when a
#       new stats snapshot arrives, and interpolated in between snapshots from
#       the live NIC counters (/proc/net/dev) anchored at the last snapshot.
#       They move EVERY refresh even if Suricata only dumps stats every 8s+.
#     * Per-cycle live delta ("+N since last refresh") shown next to them.
#   PER-COUNTER DELTAS ("+N" since the last stats tick) in EVERY section:
#     * decoder (pkts, ipv4/ipv6, tcp/udp/icmp, ARP), flow, TCP, IPS, bypass,
#       app-layer, defrag and detection counters all show what they gained at
#       the last snapshot, so you can see each counter actually working.
#   DECAY WHEN TRAFFIC LOWERS
#     * pps / Mbit/s / drops/s / alerts/s / flows/s / ARP pps no longer freeze
#       at a stale value until the next snapshot: once the socket snapshot
#       data goes stale the held rates decay x0.75 per cycle, so the numbers
#       (and only the numbers - the bars are untouched) fall smoothly when
#       traffic lowers, and rise instantly on the next live sample.
#   ARP FULLY WORKING
#     * decoder.arp now resolves on every build (extra alternatives added:
#       decoder.arp | decoder.arp_pkts | decoder.ethernet.arp), gets a live
#       per-tick delta "+N", and its own decaying "ARP rate" in the header.
#   BARS: make_graph / peak_roll / BLOCK40 logic is IDENTICAL to v1.1 - the
#     auto-scaling bars behave exactly as before.
#
# v1.1 (unchanged) highlights:
#   * counter map audited against the Suricata 7/8 stats tree, wildcard paths,
#     object-sum lookups, "n/a" for keys your build does not expose.
#   * socket rates computed over the real time between stats snapshots, NIC
#     fallback between ticks, %.0f awk output (mawk-safe).
#   * health penalties from per-cycle deltas held for HEALTH_HOLD_S seconds.
#   * flicker-free redraw, scrolling, pause, --once, --check, --debug-counters.
#
# Usage:  sudo ./suridash.sh [-i SECONDS] [--once] [--check] [--debug-counters]
#         sudo ./suridash.sh --help
# ==============================================================================

set -u

if [ "${BASH_VERSINFO[0]:-0}" -lt 4 ]; then
    echo "[-] bash >= 4 is required." >&2
    exit 1
fi

if [ -n "${LC_ALL:-}" ]; then export LANG="$LC_ALL"; unset LC_ALL; fi
export LC_NUMERIC=C

Suridash_Version="v1.2"

